5. Alternative Concept and Complexity Analysis
Let F = number of floors and S = slots per floor.
Operation	Scanning Method	Stack Method
Allocate	O(F × S)	O(1)
Release	O(1)	O(1)
Extra space	O(F × S) for slot storage	O(F × S) for free-slot stacks

Explanation:
- Scanning method checks each slot until it finds a free slot.
- Stack method maintains free slot numbers for each floor.
- Allocation takes a free slot directly from the stack.
- Release pushes the released slot number back into the stack.
- A free-slot count per floor helps identify floors with available spaces.
